		<item>
			<title>Episode 2: Where to seek help and advice if you are a model in trouble?</title>
			<itunes:summary>Emmanuel De Lange, the director of the UK Trade Union for creatives including over 1000 models among its 48000 members, explains how to seek independent advice, help and protection for everything from sexual harassment to late payments.</itunes:summary>
			<description>
The Idal Voices podcast is an educational and inspirational resource for models, designed to empower with knowledge, useful tips and inspirational stories, so that you can be on top of your career.<br />
<br />
Here is what Emmanuel and Mariya spoke about:<br />
<br />
From 01.50 - What is Equity and how it helps its model members?<br />
From 07.00 - How Equity helped models to win back over £200k of their monies in the High Court<br />
From 08.00 - How to Join Equity?<br />
From 09.20 - Why is Equity not widely known?<br />
From 10.50 - How to deal with harassment? Equity has a harassment helpline even if you are not yet a member.<br /> 
From 13.20 - How to prevent harassment.<br />
From 14.30 - What to do if you feel uncomfortable and are unsure and about whether people around you take advantage of their position?<br />
From 19.00 - How to collect monies from clients or agents that delay payment for a long time<br />
From 21.50 - When should models see their contracts with clients?<br />
From 22.40 - What if they say there was no contract?<br />
From 23.00 - Working with clients directly safely.<br />
From 24.30 - Standard contract from Equity for direct jobs - what should be there?<br />
From 26.30 - 3 tips to have a safe modelling career<br />
<br />
